From 820b90c3ec7fea876ef404da6b48e88be71fb52f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:06:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] delta bases: keep polled bases last out of the disk
 budget; don't rewrite unchanged copies

Review of ecb15dd9f0 (t_01a1d6dfe2e51725) found two fail-safe behaviour defects:

- Gateway BodyStore: a base served from memory never refreshed its file, so the disk
  budget dropped the stable, most-polled bases first and a rolled backend sent those
  reads whole. A memory hit (get, or put of a held body) now touches the file, or writes
  it again if the budget already dropped it, at most every DISK_TOUCH_S (60 s).
- Desktop DeltaBodyStore: put() marked the key dirty on every delta, including an
  unchanged body, so each polled read was rewritten whole every 2 s. An unchanged copy
  whose file already holds that hash is no longer written; its file is touched at most
  every DELTA_DISK_TOUCH_MS (60 s), and written again if the touch finds it gone.

Tests: test_a_base_memory_keeps_serving_stays_on_disk_for_the_next_backend,
test_the_disk_refresh_is_rate_limited_and_forgets_bases_memory_dropped (pytest);
'an unchanged copy is not written again', 'an unchanged copy stays recently used on
disk' (vitest).
